📌 Full Stack Authentication System (React + Node.js + MongoDB)

This is a full-stack authentication project built as part of a machine test.
It includes:

✔ User Registration
✔ User Login
✔ JWT-based Authentication
✔ Protected Dashboard Page
✔ LocalStorage persistence
✔ TailwindCSS UI
✔ Pagination
✔ Fully responsive design

The goal of this project is to demonstrate full-stack development skills including frontend, backend, API integration, authentication, and UI design.

🚀 Tech Stack Used
Frontend

React.js (Vite)

Tailwind CSS (CDN)

Axios

React Router

Backend

Node.js

Express.js

MongoDB (Mongoose)

JWT Authentication

Bcrypt Password Hashing

📂 Features
🔐 User Authentication

Register new account

Login with email & password

Password is securely hashed

Backend returns JWT token

Token + user info saved into localStorage

🔒 Protected Routes

Dashboard is accessible ONLY if:

User is logged in

JWT exists in localStorage

Unauthorized users are redirected to the login page

📊 Dashboard with User Table

After logging in, the user is redirected to the Dashboard page which includes:

A static table (as required in the assignment)

User image (auto-generated avatar)

User details like:

Name

Email

Role

Account status

Simple and clean UI design

Pagination support (Next/Previous)

🗂 LocalStorage Usage

After a successful login or registration:

The JWT token is saved

User profile data is saved

Page stays authenticated even after refresh

🛠 Installation & Setup
Clone the repository:
git clone <your-repo-url>
cd your-project-folder

⚙️ Backend Setup (Node.js)
Install dependencies:
cd server
npm install

Environment variables (.env):
PORT=5000
MONGODB_URI=your_mongo_url
JWT_SECRET=your_secret_key

Start backend:
npm run dev

🎨 Frontend Setup (React)
Install dependencies:
cd client
npm install

Start frontend:
npm run dev


Frontend runs on:

http://localhost:5173


Backend runs on:

http://localhost:5000

🌐 Deployment (Render)

This project can be hosted on Render in a single service (backend + frontend).

Just build React and serve using Express:

npm run build
npm start


Axios automatically routes to:

/api

🧠 What I Learned

Structuring a full-stack application

Using axios interceptors for token handling

Implementing secure authentication with JWT

Protecting routes using React Router

Building modern UIs with TailwindCSS

Working with MongoDB + Node.js APIs

Handling pagination & table layouts

